---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — Biggan.me"
  description="Biggan.me is an open educational scientific platform dedicated to transparent, step-by-step STEM problem solving, physical calculator bridges, and curriculum alignment."
  lang="en"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/30 text-cyan-400 text-xs font-mono">
        Institutional Profile
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">
        Democratizing Transparent STEM Education
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Bridging the divide between digital mathematical computation and physical examination hardware across South Asia and global curricula.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base space-y-6 leading-relaxed bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">1. Mission and Core Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        Mainstream computational portals function as black boxes: a user inputs numerical parameters and receives an isolated terminal number. However, academic assessment systems across secondary and university examinations require candidates to write complete intermediate algebraic derivations, unit conversions, and physical boundary conditions to secure credit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Biggan.me was built to eliminate this pedagogical gap. We provide fully exposed step-by-step solutions rendered in crisp LaTeX typography, coupled with an operational bridge to the non-programmable physical scientific calculators (such as the Casio fx-991 series) permitted inside examination halls.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-6">2. Technical Precision & Standards</h2>
      <p>
        Our computational engines utilize standardized physical and chemical constants:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Atomic Weights:</strong> Standardized IUPAC Commission on Isotopic Abundances and Atomic Weights (CIAAW).</li>
        <li><strong>Physical Constants:</strong> Committee on Data for Science and Technology (CODATA) internationally recommended values.</li>
        <li><strong>Curriculum Grounding:</strong> Strict alignment with the National Curriculum and Textbook Board (NCTB) and National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
